Chapter 4
What a bond is worth; duration; issuing and refinancing
قيمة السند ومدة ماكولاي وقرارات الإصدار وإعادة التمويل
Chapter 3 said that when the market's required return changes, a bond's price moves. This chapter computes the price, measures how far it moves, and then turns the whole subject over to the company that issued the bond: when to issue, when to refinance, and what the tax system does to both decisions.
One method does the valuation work for every instrument in this book. The value of anything that pays money over time is the present value of what it pays, discounted at the return the market requires for that risk. A bond pays coupons and a principal. Preferred stock pays a fixed dividend for ever. Common stock pays a growing dividend for ever, which is Chapter 5. The arithmetic is the same each time and only the pattern of the payments changes.
Figure F604-01 is your map.
Figure F604-01. Chapter 4 roadmap: price a bond, measure its sensitivity, then decide as the issuer.
