LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Discount"
English discount does three jobs in this chapter alone. To discount a cash flow is to compute its present value. A bond at a discount trades below par. A settlement discount is a price reduction for early payment, which Chapter 18 prices. The three are related only by the idea of something being reduced, and a candidate who reads the wrong one has misread the question rather than the calculation. Arabic uses خصم for all three as well, with the same ambiguity. French separates them usefully: actualiser for discounting a cash flow, décote for a price below par, and escompte for a settlement discount — three words where English has one, and worth borrowing as a mental distinction.
