Value of a bond | 965.35: the coupons are 50 × 3.4651 = 173.26 and the principal 1,000 × 0.7921 = 792.10, so 173.26 + 792.10 = 965.36, which rounds to 965.35 on unrounded factors.
Value of a preferred share | 40.00: 4.00 ÷ 0.10 = 40.00.
Modified duration | 3.51: 3.72 ÷ 1.06 = 3.51.
Price fall on a one-point rise | About 33.88: 965.40 × 0.0351 = 33.89, so the price falls to about 931.50.
After-tax cost of a 7% bond | 5.25 per cent: 7.0 × 0.75 = 5.25.
Refinancing payback | 3.00 years: 270,000 ÷ 90,000 = 3.00.
What it tells you | Each line is the same idea in a different dress: money arriving later is worth less, and how much less depends on the rate. The refinancing is worth doing only if more than three years remain, and the bond loses about three and a half per cent of its value for every point rates rise.
